     "text": "{\"count\": 2, \"rationale\": \"Block jumpHost:lateralMovement and iotDevice:exploitPublicApp. jumpHost feeds shareMount and is one parent of vaultRead, dbReplica and mailArchive. Blocking iotDevice cuts configSecret, so fileServer is never reached. It also cuts tokenCache, so dbLogin, hypervisor, rdpLogin and serviceAccount are never reached. That removes every remaining path to the four collection steps, so the target is unreachable. A single block is not enough: jumpHost is reachable through browserStore, which comes from entry-fed steps, and fileServer independently reaches dbReplica. No one step cuts both paths.\"}"
